  "guide": {"focus":"Two objects can have equal mass and different rotational inertia. Compare mass near the centre with mass farther out.","predict":{"prompt":"Which equal-mass disc spins more slowly after the same impulse?","options":["The hollow tube","The solid disc","They spin equally"]},"variables":[{"control":"object.properties.mass","label":"Hollow tube mass","body":"body-1-2"}],"steps":[{"text":"Run and compare the solid disc with the hollow tube."},{"text":"Inspect the compound assemblies' parts and their material densities."},{"text":"Change the hollow tube's mass, press R, and graph spin.","control":"object.properties.mass","body":"body-1-2"}],"expect":"More of the hollow tube's mass is far from its axis, giving it greater rotational inertia than the equal-mass solid disc.","limits":"Overlapping parts count shared area once. Shell thickness changes mass properties; collisions still use the outer shape."},
